Revenue and basket size

	•	Free add-on: 4+ Adult tickets in the cart → add a free audio guide or parking pass. WHEN: getTicketTitleQty("Adult") >= 4
	•	Buy X, get Y: buy 2 Adult tickets → 1 Child ticket free. This is great for family traffic.
	•	Threshold gift: cart over $100 → free gift-shop voucher or a café drink. It nudges people to add one more item.
	•	Bundle upgrade: Admission + Special Exhibit in the cart → upgrade to a "Day Pass" that includes extra amenities.

Filling slow times

	•	Off-peak perks: weekday visits before 11am, or the last 2 hours before close, earn free locker access or bonus loyalty points. This spreads crowds without cutting ticket prices.
	•	Weather-based: on rainy days, an indoor exhibit add-on is included automatically.

Customer segments

	•	Membership recognition: a logged-in member gets fast-track entry or a free guest pass automatically.
	•	Birthday month: the visitor's birthday falls within the visit date → free dessert or a souvenir.
	•	First-time visitor: no prior orders → a welcome kit or a return-visit voucher.
	•	Students, seniors, or military: a verified profile flag → priority entry or a free guided tour.

Retention and loyalty

	•	Points multiplier: double loyalty points during holidays or new exhibit launches.
	•	Return-visit voucher: completed visit → auto-issue a "come back within 30 days" pass.
	•	Milestone reward: 5th visit this year → free annual-pass upgrade trial.

Operations and goodwill

	•	Service recovery: an exhibit closed or an event cancelled → affected bookings get a free re-entry automatically.
	•	Group logistics: 15+ tickets → a free group coordinator or a reserved entry slot.
	•	Launch promotion: a new amenity in its first 2 weeks is added free to boost awareness.

Implementation idea: most of these need a new action type alongside your discount actions, such as ADD_FREE_ITEM, UPGRADE, AWARD_POINTS, ISSUE_VOUCHER, or GRANT_PERK. The WHEN side reuses what you already have (cart totals, ticket titles, quantities, categories), plus context facts like visit date/time, customer profile, and weather.
